    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b9168f555be34ae79912c571efaee12d",
      "statement": "The two redaction helpers have deliberate coverage limits that shape how the rest of the service must behave: `redact_url`/`redact_text` only recognise the literal `scheme://user:password@` userinfo form (a colon-less `https://TOKEN@host/...` or an scp-style `git@host:org/repo.git` remote passes through untouched), and the auth-header pass masks only the single whitespace-delimited token after `authorization`/`private-token`, so the literal-secret pass — or never composing an authenticated URL — remains the real guarantee.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/core/util.py#L8-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:11265ab274f35309ea6e32dd4b5ae6db0843514610716cd19e5351b01f0be4fe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1288ad08697142269192e72bc10034c6",
      "statement": "Failure text stored on the job is bounded twice after redaction and never reformatted: `run_git` raises `IngestionError` carrying only the last eight lines of `stderr` (or `stdout`), which `run_git_status` already redacted, and `WorkerLoop._run` persists it truncated to 500 characters in `error` and in `push_result['detail']`, so truncation cannot re-expose a redacted value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/services/ingestion.py#L142-L164",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:712e11bed9725ff47c3f5131f298e1a53a9db1a5f682cf109effe428bf833bf6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/worker/loop.py#L104-L126",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6b4f7b00249c632fcbc70080b3c5ced80cfcc62df56fd2023fd9732144d10555:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_26a9800a67944b40bb35c92b8161c9f0",
      "statement": "The OpenAI-compatible loopback proxy is a redaction and environment boundary: `start_proxy` runs uvicorn with `access_log=False` so injected extra headers and upstream traffic never reach the worker's own logs, the forward app strips hop-by-hop headers in both directions, and `/health/model` probes the configured base URL directly instead of the proxy.",
